From c345e847168bab137a649ec16dbd0acdeee8f855 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:02:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 64/65] MAS local: lay out the resize inode the way online
 resize expects

inode_attach_resize put reserved GDT block r at double-indirect slot
(r + bg_desc_blocks) modulo bg_desc_reserve_blocks. The kernel's online
resize (reserve_backup_gdb, add_new_gdb) and e2fsprogs use the modulo of
the slots per block instead. The two agree only when the reserve is a
full block of slots (1024 with 4 KiB blocks, any file system of more than
128 groups). With less, e.g. a 16 GB data partition (1023 reserved
blocks), the last reserved block lands in slot 0. Growing such a
partition online then stops at the first new group that carries a
superblock backup: "reserve_backup_gdb: reserved block 1024 not at
offset 1023", leaving 16 GB grown to 30.4 GB instead of 32 GB.

e2fsck only checks the first quarter of the slots, so it never reported
it. Data partitions created before this keep the old layout.

Change-Id: Id5c3e6fa90a6d17a4b6b951f691fe48c2424098a
---
 android/third_party/ext4_utils/src/indirect.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/third_party/ext4_utils/src/indirect.c b/android/third_party/ext4_utils/src/indirect.c
index 56f26d03d..d26bc605f 100644
--- a/android/third_party/ext4_utils/src/indirect.c
+++ b/android/third_party/ext4_utils/src/indirect.c
@@ -454,10 +454,16 @@ void inode_attach_resize(struct ext4_inode *inode,
 			info.block_size * info.bg_desc_reserve_blocks,
 			get_block(alloc, 0));
 
-	for (i = 0; i < info.bg_desc_reserve_blocks; i++) {
-		int r = (i - aux_info.bg_desc_blocks) % info.bg_desc_reserve_blocks;
-		if (r < 0)
-			r += info.bg_desc_reserve_blocks;
+	/* Reserved GDT block r sits at double-indirect slot (bg_desc_blocks + r) modulo
+	 * the slots per block, which is where the kernel's online resize
+	 * (reserve_backup_gdb, add_new_gdb) and e2fsprogs look for it. Taking the modulo
+	 * of bg_desc_reserve_blocks instead only agrees when that is a full block of
+	 * slots: with fewer (any file system of 128 groups or less, e.g. a 16 GB data
+	 * partition) the last reserved block lands in slot 0, and an online resize
+	 * stops at the first new group that carries a superblock backup ("reserved
+	 * block ... not at offset ..."). */
+	for (u32 r = 0; r < info.bg_desc_reserve_blocks; r++) {
+		i = (aux_info.bg_desc_blocks + r) % aux_info.blocks_per_ind;
 
 		dind_block_data[i] = get_block(alloc, r);
 
